BOOKMARKS
=========

- https://pll.harvard.edu/course/cs50-introduction-computer-science — Introductory Harvard course covering core computer science concepts and programming fundamentals
- https://teachyourselfcs.com — Structured self-study roadmap to learn computer science fundamentals independently
- https://sarabander.github.io/sicp/html/index.xhtml — Online version of Structure and Interpretation of Computer Programs
- https://softwarefoundations.cis.upenn.edu — Interactive series on logic, formal verification, and programming language theory
- https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu — Complete Feynman Lectures on Physics covering fundamental physics concepts
- https://www.nand2tetris.org — Hands-on course building a computer system from logic gates to high-level software
- https://missing.csail.mit.edu — Practical guide to essential developer tools like shell, git, and scripting
- https://craftinginterpreters.com — Step-by-step guide to building interpreters and programming languages
- https://aalhour.com/awesome-compilers — Curated list of compiler design resources and tools
- https://www.cprogramming.com — Tutorials and references for learning C and C++ programming
- https://seenaburns.com/building-c-programs — Guide to compiling and structuring C programs
- https://swc.rs — High-performance Rust-based JavaScript/TypeScript compiler and tooling
- https://projecteuler.net/archives — Archive of mathematical and algorithmic programming challenges
- https://open.kattis.com/problems — Large collection of competitive programming problems
- https://adventofcode.com — Annual programming challenge series with daily puzzles
- https://adventjs.dev/es — JavaScript/TypeScript coding challenges focused on problem solving
- https://visualgo.net/en — Interactive visualizations of data structures and algorithms
- https://samwho.dev/big-o — Visual explanation of Big-O time and space complexity
- https://projectbook.code.brettchalupa.com/_introduction.html — Collection of practical coding project ideas
- https://vite.dev — Fast modern frontend build tool and development server
- https://www.solidjs.com — Reactive UI library for building high-performance web interfaces
- https://qwik.dev — Resumable web framework optimized for instant loading
- https://freecomputerbooks.com/ — Directory of free programming and computer science books
- https://tanstack.com — Collection of high-quality TypeScript/JavaScript libraries
- https://zod.dev — TypeScript-first schema validation and parsing library
- https://jotai.org — Minimal atomic state management library for React
- https://zustand-demo.pmnd.rs — Lightweight and scalable state management solution
- https://storybook.js.org — Tool for building and testing UI components in isolation
- https://www.better-auth.com — Modern authentication and user management solution
- https://animejs.com — Lightweight JavaScript animation library
- https://tauri.app — Framework for building desktop apps using Rust and web technologies
- https://wails.io — Build desktop applications using Go and web frontend
- https://neutralino.js.org — Ultra-lightweight framework for desktop apps with web technologies
- http://www.lazyvim.org — Fast and modular Neovim configuration framework
- https://github.com/doomemacs/doomemacs — Highly optimized and modular Emacs configuration
- https://neomutt.org — Feature-rich command-line email client
- https://newsboat.org — Command-line RSS/Atom feed reader
- https://www.hackthebox.com — Platform offering hands-on penetration testing labs
- https://tryhackme.com — Beginner-friendly cybersecurity training and guided labs
- https://www.vulnhub.com — Collection of vulnerable virtual machines for security practice
- https://book.hacktricks.wiki/en/index.html — Comprehensive wiki of hacking techniques and methodologies
- https://lawsofux.com — Collection of psychological principles applied to UX design
- https://www.pencil.dev — Open-source tool for UI/UX prototyping and design
- https://excalidraw.com — Collaborative whiteboard with a hand-drawn visual style
- https://github.com/gohugoio/hugo — Fast static site generator written in Go
- https://github.com/withastro/starlight — Documentation framework built on Astro
- https://github.com/mkdocs/mkdocs — Static site generator for project documentation using Markdown
- https://github.com/rust-lang/mdBook — Tool for creating books from Markdown files
- https://news.ycombinator.com — Community-driven tech and startup news aggregator
- https://blog.acolyer.org — Summaries and reviews of important computer science research papers
- https://dev.to — Social platform for developers to share articles and knowledge
- https://github.com/manjunath5496 — Repository collection of programming resources and books
- https://www.jscamp.dev/ — Interactive JavaScript learning platform with exercises
- https://craftinginterpreters.com/ — Comprehensive guide to building interpreters (duplicate link)
- https://learnxinyminutes.com/ — Learn programming languages quickly with concise examples
- https://thepythonbook.com/ — Free Python programming book for beginners
- https://roadmap.sh/ — Visual roadmaps for learning different tech roles and skills
- https://github.com/trys/sergey — Personal repository with curated technical resources
- https://github.com/manjunath5496 — Collection of programming books and materials (duplicate link)
- https://github.com/practical-tutorials/project-based-learning — List of programming tutorials organized by building projects
- https://caniuse.com/ — Browser compatibility tables for web technologies
- https://github.com/steipete — Developer repositories and open-source contributions
- https://github.com/uzbl/uzbl — Minimalist and hackable web browser project
- https://softwarefoundations.cis.upenn.edu/ — Formal methods and verification course materials (duplicate link)
- https://suckless.org/ — Minimalist software philosophy and tools (e.g., dwm, st)
- https://www.teamten.com/lawrence/style/ — Guidelines for clear technical writing and documentation
- https://www.py4e.com/ — Python for Everybody course focused on practical programming
- https://learn-anything.xyz/ — Visual knowledge graphs for learning various topics
- https://github.com/w3c — Official repositories for web standards organization
- https://fullstackopen.com/en/ — Full-stack web development course using modern JavaScript
- https://courses.mooc.fi/org/uh-cs/courses/full-stack-open-nextjs — Advanced full-stack course focused on Next.js
